# PV18: relative energies of polymorph pairs of molecular crystals.
#
# Each block is E(cry-2)/Z2 - E(cry-1)/Z1, i.e. the electronic energy
# difference per molecule between the two polymorphs, matching the dE
# column of 25_pv18/summary.org (which is in kJ/mol; converted here to
# kcal/mol with 1 kcal = 4.184 kJ).
#
# The name says 18 but the set contains 19 pairs.
#
# The energies are B86bPBE-XDM, calculated with Quantum ESPRESSO. The
# vibrational (dFvib) and free-energy (dG) columns of summary.org are not
# reproducible from single-point energies and are not included here.
#
# Structures: 25_pv18/<refcode>/<refcode>.scf.in
# Each block carries the pair refcode as a label after the reference value
# (the default fieldasrxn=999 picks it up for eval output).
#
